# The only .dockerignore Docker reads for the Python services: every one of them
# builds with `context: .` (this directory) in docker-compose.yaml, and Docker
# applies the file at the context root, never one beside the Dockerfile. Patterns
# are rooted here, so anything excluded at any depth needs the `**/` prefix.
# crewdb and frontend use their own context and keep their own file.

# Secrets and local environment
**/.env

# Virtual environments
ENV
*/.venv
**/venv
**/*venv
**/*venvs

# Python build and tool caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Editor state
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Tests
**/tests
**/conftest.py
**/pytest.ini

# Local runtime artifacts (all gitignored)
**/executions
**/demo_stands
**/*_stand
**/staticfiles
**/media
**/graph_data
